+## Completion and evidence maintenance (2026-11-04)
+
+The original experiment is complete as recorded on the author's M4 Mac mini. Its historical records, frozen configuration and benchmark are retained. Missing weights in a copied project do not mean the original experiment was unfinished.
+
+The current copy's locked environment and raw/processed data can be restored separately. Source downloads can be verified against the original SHA-256 list. Training/export/evaluation now check required artifacts before resuming, and refuse to silently retrain over orphan historical JSON records. `MIBCI_DATA_DIR` and `MIBCI_RESULTS_DIR` isolate fresh reproductions. An already frozen analysis cannot be refrozen or have its epoch budget silently changed.
+
+A matched-budget supplementary pruning comparison gives the unpruned and pruned branches the same 100 extra epochs. It was added after test results were known, cannot change the historical finalist, and labels independently rebuilt weights explicitly. Its actual execution status and commands are recorded in `docs/WORK_LOG.md`; see the generated report for verified results rather than treating the existence of a script as an executed experiment.
+
+```bash
+python3 scripts/audit_project.py --deep
+.venv.nosync/bin/python -m unittest discover -s tests -v
+.venv.nosync/bin/python scripts/build_report.py
+python3 scripts/build_presentation.py
+```
+
+The historical INT8 `input_bytes` values use a modeled one-byte representation. The updated benchmark separates this from actual float32 graph-interface inputs. `scripts/benchmark_memory.py` measures isolated-process RSS when model exports are available; this also is not MCU SRAM. The original pruning comparison has extra-training confounding; use the matched-budget supplementary analysis for the corresponding controlled contrast.
+
+### Completed supplementary result
+
+The post-test M5 reproduction completed 54 bases and 162 matched-budget branches, with FP32/INT8 evaluation of all 216 models. At relevance-16 INT8, 50% pruning loses **1.56 percentage points** against the equally fine-tuned unpruned model (95% participant bootstrap interval **−2.86 to −0.42**). This qualifies the original near-baseline mean: pruning is not necessarily accuracy-free. The original M4 results and finalist are retained. See the report and `results/supplementary/matched_budget/` for all contrasts and provenance.
+
+Isolated M5 ONNX Runtime process peaks are around 57–59 MiB, including interpreter/runtime overhead. They do not verify the modeled 5.5x activation ratio or MCU SRAM. Portable FP32/INT8 predictions were checked against all 288 predictions of the corresponding supplementary evaluation.
